1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:45,964
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,091 --> 00:00:48,317
=Episode 9=

4
00:00:56,079 --> 00:00:56,840
Ms. Su.

5
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:00,884
Actually...

6
00:01:00,896 --> 00:01:01,425
The rain has stopped.

7
00:01:06,039 --> 00:01:07,000
Your clothes are soaked, Mr. Gu.

8
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,079
You should head back.

9
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:08,840
Don't catch a cold.

10
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:15,640
All right.

11
00:01:16,359 --> 00:01:16,920
Then...

12
00:01:18,159 --> 00:01:18,680
I'll get going.

13
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:30,560
Mr. Gu.

14
00:01:36,079 --> 00:01:37,200
Will you come back?

15
00:01:39,159 --> 00:01:39,680
Wait for me.

16
00:01:51,239 --> 00:01:51,879
Wanniang.

17
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,760
If I've counted right,

18
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,760
His Majesty is leaving tomorrow.

19
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:56,680
Will he...

20
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,560
take you back to the palace?

21
00:01:59,159 --> 00:02:01,319
With that jealous consort around,

22
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:03,400
Xiao Che would never.

23
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,319
Then wouldn't you be

24
00:02:05,719 --> 00:02:07,400
like a roadside wildflower,

25
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,879
blooming only to wither?

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,980
Then I'll have that jealous consort

27
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:16,000
pluck this wildflower herself

28
00:02:17,039 --> 00:02:18,240
and bring it back to the palace.

29
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,840
(Qiluo Silk Shop)
(His Majesty keeps going out.)

30
00:02:24,439 --> 00:02:25,719
(We're about to return to the palace,)

31
00:02:25,719 --> 00:02:26,919
(yet he's nowhere to be seen.)

32
00:02:27,879 --> 00:02:29,120
(Let's see)

33
00:02:29,719 --> 00:02:30,680
(just what it is)

34
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:31,759
(that's got him so spellbound.)

35
00:02:37,639 --> 00:02:38,120
Get out.

36
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,400
Where's your grown-up?

37
00:02:52,479 --> 00:02:53,199
My sister's out

38
00:02:53,639 --> 00:02:54,960
gathering herbs.

39
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,039
Your Highness.

40
00:02:58,919 --> 00:02:59,719
We found His Majesty.

41
00:03:00,439 --> 00:03:01,639
He's waiting in the carriage
to return to the palace with you.

42
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:02,639
Let's go.

43
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,039
You left Guizhen Cottage today.

44
00:03:14,919 --> 00:03:16,240
You found out quickly, Your Majesty.

45
00:03:16,879 --> 00:03:18,039
I heard

46
00:03:18,199 --> 00:03:19,080
there are flowers outside the palace

47
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,439
that are rare inside the palace.

48
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,479
They may look plain,

49
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,840
but they're strangely captivating.

50
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,520
I got curious,

51
00:03:28,919 --> 00:03:30,120
so I went to see for myself

52
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,800
just how special

53
00:03:33,319 --> 00:03:34,599
those flowers really are.

54
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,280
(Physician)

55
00:03:50,319 --> 00:03:51,360
Since when did you

56
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,680
start believing such nonsense?

57
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:53,879
It's only a rumor.

58
00:03:54,719 --> 00:03:55,919
If Your Majesty says there aren't any,

59
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:57,919
then of course

60
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:00,159
I believe you.

61
00:04:51,503 --> 00:04:53,549
(Three Poems by Wang Wei, Including
"Autumn Evening in the Mountains")

62
00:05:10,959 --> 00:05:11,800
(Mr. Gu.)

63
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,920
(Will you come back?)

64
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:29,279
Your Majesty.

65
00:05:29,879 --> 00:05:30,480
Your Majesty.

66
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:32,360
As you ordered,

67
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,439
I brought back

68
00:05:33,759 --> 00:05:34,560
what you asked for.

69
00:05:44,759 --> 00:05:45,600
Did the stall owner

70
00:05:45,879 --> 00:05:46,680
say anything?

71
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,279
At first,

72
00:05:47,519 --> 00:05:49,800
she wouldn't give it to me.

73
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,839
She said she'd woven it
for someone in particular,

74
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,319
and wouldn't give it to anyone else.

75
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:54,720
Then

76
00:05:55,199 --> 00:05:57,199
I showed her the woven grasshopper.

77
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:58,920
Only then did she ask

78
00:05:59,439 --> 00:06:00,600
if Mr. Gu had sent me.

79
00:06:01,279 --> 00:06:02,040
What else did she say?

80
00:06:04,079 --> 00:06:05,919
She was delighted

81
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,839
and said Mr. Gu was very thoughtful.

82
00:06:08,399 --> 00:06:11,000
She figured Mr. Gu must be busy

83
00:06:11,279 --> 00:06:12,240
and couldn't visit often.

84
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:13,639
After thinking it over,

85
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,839
she gave me something to bring back

86
00:06:16,279 --> 00:06:17,319
for Mr. Gu.

87
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,199
She said

88
00:06:26,839 --> 00:06:27,560
Mr. Gu should

89
00:06:27,759 --> 00:06:29,160
take good care of himself.

90
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:32,879
What else?

91
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:34,240
She also said

92
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,680
this was

93
00:06:36,199 --> 00:06:37,480
a token of her longing for you.

94
00:06:44,639 --> 00:06:46,319
Come with me to the West Buddhist Hall.

95
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,720
We'll hear my uncle expound the sutras.

96
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,199
Yes.

97
00:07:09,989 --> 00:07:14,176
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

98
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:17,923
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

99
00:07:18,158 --> 00:07:20,757
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

100
00:07:20,794 --> 00:07:23,074
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

101
00:07:23,121 --> 00:07:26,950
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

102
00:07:27,352 --> 00:07:30,705
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

103
00:07:31,632 --> 00:07:35,145
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

104
00:07:35,645 --> 00:07:38,212
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

105
00:07:38,338 --> 00:07:40,371
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

106
00:07:40,438 --> 00:07:44,215
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

107
00:07:44,565 --> 00:07:48,898
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

108
00:07:49,121 --> 00:07:52,628
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

109
00:07:52,809 --> 00:07:55,662
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

110
00:07:55,729 --> 00:08:01,343
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

111
00:08:01,383 --> 00:08:04,397
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

112
00:08:04,438 --> 00:08:10,446
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

113
00:08:11,113 --> 00:08:18,068
♪The past has faded away♪

114
00:08:18,068 --> 00:08:22,068
♪The past has faded away♪
